{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837042",
      "title": "Revisiting the \"Rules of Hooks\" & Why To Use Hooks",
      "sourceHash": "7b05beab563a6ab6c0db3b63e3e7cad9dd6ef754433b5b54de2375737bdc2e67",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.42,
          "end": 2.94,
          "en": "Now before we'll explore the concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.94,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "of custom Hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "I wanna repeat the rules of Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 9.837,
          "en": "Two important rules you must be aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.837,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "of when working with Hooks in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "And here the first rule is that you must only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "use React Hooks inside of React Component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 26.06,
          "en": "And the second rule is that those Hooks must not be nested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "in if statements nested functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 32.313,
          "en": "for loops or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "But now we'll actually change that first rule a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "because it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "that this first rule is actually a bit more flexible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 47.52,
          "en": "because you are actually not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.52,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "to just using React Hooks inside of Component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "Instead, you may also use them inside of other Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 58.413,
          "en": "so inside of custom Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 62.76,
          "en": "So Hooks may be used inside of Component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.76,
          "end": 65.49,
          "en": "or inside of other Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.49,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "That's an important variation of this first rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "and it's this variation that enables us to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "custom Hooks, as you will see throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "But why would you build custom Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 81.93299999999999,
          "en": "and what should these custom Hooks do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "Well, the idea behind building custom Hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "is always to wrap and reuse code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 93.363,
          "en": "that goes into your Component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "For example, here in the App.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 99.393,
          "en": "in this project I provided to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.32,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "There, I got this useEffect Hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "where I in the end send an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "and where I manage some loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 111.333,
          "en": "and potentially an error state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 116.28,
          "en": "And if you take a look at this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.28,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "and you then take a look at the code in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "AvailablePlaces.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 125.34,
          "en": "you will notice that the code is quite similar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.34,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "It's not exactly equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "we are sending different requests to different URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 134.04,
          "en": "and here in AvailablePlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.04,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "we are then also transforming the data we're getting back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "but the main idea is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 142.44,
          "en": "We're sending an HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.44,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "we're managing some loading state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "we're managing some error state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 149.673,
          "en": "and we're using useEffect for all that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 154.38,
          "en": "And this would be an example for some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 157.41,
          "en": "that we might want to outsource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.41,
          "end": 161.91,
          "en": "and make more generic so that we can reuse it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "so that we don't have to write this similar code twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 170.76,
          "en": "in two different Components, but so that we maybe have one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 173.85,
          "en": "reusable configurable function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.85,
          "end": 176.55,
          "en": "that could be used in both Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "Because, of course, you might remember",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 180.96,
          "en": "that the idea behind Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.96,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "was to reuse Logic and JSX structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "as we're doing it here with the modal, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "we are reusing this Component with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 196.65,
          "en": "And just as this was the idea behind Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.65,
          "end": 200.22,
          "en": "we might want to reuse other code as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.22,
          "end": 203.25,
          "en": "code that does not return JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.25,
          "end": 206.85,
          "en": "so that can't go into its own Component, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.85,
          "end": 208.203,
          "en": "Code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.1,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "this useEffect call with the logic inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 214.65,
          "en": "we might want to reuse that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.65,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "but we can't put it into a separate Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 220.59,
          "en": "because this is just a part of a Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.59,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "It does not return JSX code or anything like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "and therefore this is the kind of problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "we can solve with custom React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "Now of course, we could also try to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 235.56,
          "en": "outsource and reuse code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "by grabbing it and putting it into a separate function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.33,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "a function which we could call fetchData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 246.57,
          "en": "and which we could define in any file we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.57,
          "end": 249.69,
          "en": "And then we could try to call fetchData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.69,
          "end": 253.3,
          "en": "in every Component that needs that functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 258.15,
          "en": "because that is how you normally outsource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.15,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "logic in programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 263.7,
          "en": "and JavaScript programming is, of course, no exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.7,
          "end": 267.18,
          "en": "If you have some logic that needs to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.18,
          "end": 270.81,
          "en": "in different places, you put it into a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.81,
          "end": 275.79,
          "en": "and that function can then be used in different places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 280.56,
          "en": "Just as we created this fetchUserPlaces function before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.56,
          "end": 284.1,
          "en": "which does contain that reusable code for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.1,
          "end": 286.533,
          "en": "fetching this userPlaces data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 290.25,
          "en": "But this does not work here because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "the code which I wanna outsource and share",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 297.09000000000003,
          "en": "actually uses Hooks inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.09000000000003,
          "end": 300.45,
          "en": "and it also needs to manipulate state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.45,
          "end": 304.35,
          "en": "And these are things which can only be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.35,
          "end": 309.033,
          "en": "inside of Components, not in some random shared function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.87,
          "end": 314.22,
          "en": "Sure, here I'm using this function in a Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.22,
          "end": 317.88,
          "en": "but there is no guarantee that I'll always use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 317.88,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "fetchData just in a Component and nowhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "And if I would use it somewhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 326.28,
          "en": "all this code here would fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 326.28,
          "end": 329.52,
          "en": "because Hooks can only be used in Components in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 329.52,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "and state updates therefore can also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 334.743,
          "en": "only be made in Component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.39,
          "end": 340.02,
          "en": "And that's why this will not be a valid solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 340.02,
          "end": 342.33,
          "en": "and why I'll roll back this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.33,
          "end": 344.76,
          "en": "and go back to the code I had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 344.76,
          "end": 348.84000000000003,
          "en": "And that's exactly why we need this custom Hooks feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 348.84000000000003,
          "end": 351.72,
          "en": "I'll introduce you to in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 351.72,
          "end": 355.71,
          "en": "because custom Hooks will also be functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 355.71,
          "end": 359.37,
          "en": "that we can then call from different places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 359.37,
          "end": 363.21,
          "en": "but they will be functions that are guaranteed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 363.21,
          "end": 365.25,
          "en": "to be used in valid places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 365.25,
          "end": 369.573,
          "en": "so that are guaranteed to be used in Components in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}